                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238172990",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198025540634",
                            "num_reviews": 354,
                            "playtime_forever": 352,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 129,
                            "deck_playtime_at_review": 129,
                            "last_played": 1792597066
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I don't think I've been more annoyed by a puzzle game. It's not difficult in the sense that you can't figure out what to do. The problem is how dark it is and the one-hit-kills from the ghosts. \nYou can be in total darkness, light your match and still just die instantly because you accidentally walked face first into a ghost. Of course I didn't see it - it was too dark. The game doesn't even give a \"mash to escape\" or something? And checkpoints are very rare - you have to save constantly, and if you forgot, then you can lose a lot of time repeating sections. And the inconsistent camera angles that seem to be made to disorient you as much as possible don't help in avoiding the ghosts. \nAnd the damn matches! Sometimes, you light a match and it burns your hand - forcing you to light another match. This RNG can trigger multiple times - meaning you could be on your last 3 matches and get screwed by RNG into a game over. \nIn a way, the design perfectly matches the feeling of an oppressive haunted house - but It's just so annoying.",
